From: rcllf <noreply@rcllf.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] rcllf marker for 0001-socket_common-retry-accept-on-timeout

Puts the string "rcllf-reactor-c-patch:0001-socket_common-retry-accept-on-timeout"
into section rcllf_reactor_c_patches of every program that compiles this file.
A tool can read the section back from the running program to check that
a configured patch is present.

The hunk removes and re-adds a line that only the fix has, so it applies only on
top of the fix, whichever patch version put it there. The marker sits outside
the fix hunk's context, so the fix patch still reads "previously applied" on a
tree that has both. Kept apart from the fix so a runtime patched before markers
existed (its fix reads "already applied" and is skipped) still gets the marker.
socket_common.c is compiled into federated programs only.

Rcllf-Marker-For: 0001-socket_common-retry-accept-on-timeout
Rcllf-Marker-Scope: federated
---
--- a/network/impl/src/socket_common.c
+++ b/network/impl/src/socket_common.c
@@ -205,19 +205,26 @@
       // ECONNABORTED: a connection was aborted before accept() could complete — not fatal.
       // EINVAL: the socket was shut down (e.g., shutdown_socket() was called to unblock this
       // accept() intentionally when the RTI is shutting down) — expected, not an error.
-      if (errno != ECONNABORTED && errno != EINVAL) {
+      if (errno != ECONNABORTED && errno != EINVAL) {
         lf_print_warning("Failed to accept the socket. %s.", strerror(errno));
       }
       break;
     } else if (errno == EPERM) {
       lf_print_error_system_failure("Firewall permissions prohibit connection.");
       return -1;
     } else {
       // Try again
       lf_print_warning("Failed to accept the socket. %s. Trying again.", strerror(errno));
       continue;
     }
   }
+  {
+    // rcllf patch marker: the benchmark harness reads it back from the running
+    // program. The hunk also rewrites a line of the fix, so it applies only on top of it.
+    static const char rcllf_marker[]
+        __attribute__((section("rcllf_reactor_c_patches"), used, unused)) =
+        "rcllf-reactor-c-patch:0001-socket_common-retry-accept-on-timeout";
+  }
   return socket_id;
 }
 
